's all-time high is 110\u00b0F, on June 20, 2008.","t_chg":"Santa Maria's nights got warmer. Its days didn't.","p_chg":"Across 112 complete years: Santa Maria's average low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.24\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.15 to +0.32), about +2.8\u00b0F since 1906. Santa Maria's average high shows no clear change: +0.02\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.08 to +0.11) that includes zero.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 9 of 12 months. Highs rose in 1 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Santa Maria's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (\u22120.22 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 13.3 inches a year. The wettest year was 1941 (33.51 in); the driest, 2013 (2.99 in). Santa Maria almost never sees snow (the 1991\u20132020 average is 0.0 inches a winter), so there's no snowfall chart.","show_snow":false,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 13 daily record highs, no daily record lows"}}